                            <comment id="310185" author="adilger" created="Fri, 13 Aug 2021 18:10:43 +0000">&lt;p&gt;I wonder if this may happen if a &lt;tt&gt;stack_trap&lt;/tt&gt; registered by this subtest returns a non-zero value, since those are run after the test sub shell exits, but before the test is "finished"?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="310219" author="adilger" created="Sat, 14 Aug 2021 06:50:14 +0000">&lt;p&gt;I also saw this same failure on sanity test_398b - finished with "&lt;tt&gt;waited for trevis-39vm11 network 5s&lt;/tt&gt;" then failed with "&lt;tt&gt;returned 1&lt;/tt&gt;". &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="310397" author="zam" created="Tue, 17 Aug 2021 12:55:48 +0000">&lt;p&gt;sanity test 4, the same failure w/o obvious reason&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/cb7fa77c-c447-4af8-8294-6846c61a7019" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/cb7fa77c-c447-4af8-8294-6846c61a7019&lt;/a&gt; .&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="310621" author="emoly.liu" created="Thu, 19 Aug 2021 03:41:13 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Maybe this issue is related to the recent commit 67752f6d at &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/44033" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/44033&lt;/a&gt;, and seems it only happens to group review-ldiskfs-arm, especially on MDS1.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The t-f change shows:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
 check_node_health() {
        local nodes=${1:-$(comma_list $(nodes_list))}
-
-       &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; node in ${nodes&lt;span class="code-comment"&gt;//,/ }; &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;do&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;-               check_network &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"$node"&lt;/span&gt; 5
-               &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; [ $? -eq 0 ]; then
-                       do_node $node &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"$LCTL get_param catastrophe 2&amp;gt;&amp;amp;1"&lt;/span&gt; |
-                               grep -q &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"catastrophe=1"&lt;/span&gt; &amp;amp;&amp;amp;
-                               error &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"$node:LBUG/LASSERT detected"&lt;/span&gt; || &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
-               fi
-       done
+       local health=$TMP/node_health.$$
+
+       do_nodes $nodes &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"$LCTL get_param catastrophe 2&amp;gt;&amp;amp;1"&lt;/span&gt; | tee $health |
+               grep &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"catastrophe=1"&lt;/span&gt; &amp;amp;&amp;amp; error &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"LBUG/LASSERT detected"&lt;/span&gt;
+       # Only check/report network health &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; get_param isn't reported, since
+       # *clearly* the network is working &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; get_param returned something.
+       &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (( $(grep -c catastro $health) != $(wc -w &amp;lt;&amp;lt;&amp;lt; ${nodes&lt;span class="code-comment"&gt;//,/ }) )); then
&lt;/span&gt;+               &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; node in ${nodes&lt;span class="code-comment"&gt;//,/}; &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;do&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;+                       check_network $node 5
+               done
+       fi
+       rm -f $health
 }

check_network() {
        local host=$1
        local max=$2
        local sleep=${3:-5}

        [ &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"$host"&lt;/span&gt; = &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"$HOSTNAME"&lt;/span&gt; ] &amp;amp;&amp;amp; &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; 0

        &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; ! wait_for_function --quiet &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"ping -c 1 -w 3 $host"&lt;/span&gt; $max $sleep; then
                echo &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"$(date +&lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;'%H:%M:%S (%s)'&lt;/span&gt;) waited &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; $host network ${max}s"&lt;/span&gt;
                exit 1
        fi
}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="310680" author="adilger" created="Thu, 19 Aug 2021 18:04:37 +0000">&lt;p&gt;I was wondering the same about 44033, but that patch only landed 2 days ago and failures on master have been happening for at least 6 days when this ticket was opened. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
